A||N||7||pherder||When it rains, it pours ...||||8||
Z||000000||pherder||09-08-2000||02:59 PM||||Well I was taking my 88 Coupe (see It drives!!! ...) to the local Highway Patrol station to have it inspected (it is an out of state car and has to be inspected before it can be titled in Kansas).  <P>I put in on my two wheel dolly (not legal to drive in on the streets) so that I could drag it to the inspection station.  About 2 miles from my house I feel a strange movement in the truck and look out the rear view window and see SMOKE!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>Pull off the road and go back to the car and the right rear tire is flat.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>I proceed to get out the necessary tools to change the tire for the spare.  Of course the spare is low but I decide to use it anyway.  Take off the tire and I see this!<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=208525&a=1537447&p=27945976&Sequence=0"> <P>and<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=208525&a=1537447&p=27945975&Sequence=0"> <P>Holy @#$#@!$ !!!!<P>I take off the rotor and secure the caliper so that it will not get in the way.  Put on the spare and carefully drag the car back home.<P>When I get the car up on jacks, and get the damaged pieces off, I find the following:<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=208525&a=1537447&p=27945974&Sequence=0"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=208525&a=1537447&p=27945973&Sequence=0"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=208525&a=1537447&p=27945972&Sequence=0"> <P>I am glad I saved the parts off the Formula I stripped.  Had a rebuild kit for the caliper so I rebuilt one of the spares and used a good rotor and put everything back together.<P>You can't see it in the picture very well but the tire is holed completely thru.  The wheel has grind marks on the inside but nothing deep so I can use the wheel again but the caliper and the upright are trash.  It even broke the brand new brake pads!<P>The only thing I can figure happened is I lost the lower caliper mounting bolt.  I hadn't locktight it, I guess but it is now!<P>If it wasn't for bad luck, I would have NO luck with this car!!!<P>Paul||||reg||8
Z||000001||mrfiero||09-08-2000||03:54 PM||||Ouch!  I had this happen to me while driving.  I had just replaced the right front caliper with a rebuilt one from the Fiero Store and I was cruising on the highway and took the exit ramp.  I tapped the brakes to start to slow down and I felt something give and the front end locked up.<P>I limped it to the truck stop on the corner and pulled off the wheel.  I saw what you saw, except my rotor was in 3 or 4 pieces.  <P>I too learned the hard way about using LockTite on the threads!||||reg||11
Z||000002||TheFiero64||09-08-2000||04:38 PM||||I also had one of those bolts come out on me wile going down the highway <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">. I had to limp home without using the brakes. It didn't break anything thank god, But I always use threadlock now.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000003||Monkeyman||09-08-2000||08:49 PM||||Hmmm...Maybe I'll add some Threadlock this weekend when I replace the brake lines.  Never knew something like that could happen.||||reg||1
Z||000004||TheFiero64||09-09-2000||01:01 PM||||I would Monkeyman, You never can be too careful. I learned the hard way.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||09-09-2000||01:57 PM||||I'll be doing the brake lines tomorrow if it doesn't rain.  (Imight even do them if it does rain since my car is starting to pull.  Might be a small leak in one of the lines.)||||reg||1
Z||000006||Coconut||09-09-2000||05:36 PM||||Pherder, <BR>Thanks for posting this. Like MM I'm in the middle of doing some brake work as well and I am certainly going to make sure the Caliper mounting bolts get some LockTite on the threads before reinstallation. Sorry that had to happen to ya but glad to see the damage was at least minimal. Thanks for sharing.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Coconut's_Signature_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||rprevo||09-10-2000||12:08 AM|||| Make sure it is removable thread locker!<BR>Permanent locktight will really suck when<BR>you try to break the caliper loose,<P>Ray<BR>||||reg||1
